## 2. State Structure for Dynamic Checklist Templates

The checklist state will transition from a flat index-based array to an ID-based object to support polymorphic JSONB storage.

**Template Definition Structure:**
```javascript
const FLEETS = {
  "Challenger": [
    {
      section_id: "CHL-SEC1",
      title: "Front Fuselage",
      items: [
        { id: "CHL-FF-A1", description: "Static Ports check..." },
        { 
          id: "CHL-FF-D2", 
          description: "Record NLG Tire #1 Pressure",
          meta_entry: { type: "numeric", unit: "psi" } 
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "Hawker": [ /* ... */ ],
  "Gulfstream": [ /* ... existing ... */ ]
}
```

**Frontend Reactivity State:**
We will introduce a `metaValues` object to track numeric/date inputs alongside the existing `marks` and `comments`.
```javascript
let currentFleet = "Gulfstream"; // Active template
let marks = {};      // e.g., { "CHL-FF-A1-eng": true }
let comments = {};   // e.g., { "CHL-FF-A1": "Slight wear noticed" }
let metaValues = {}; // e.g., { "CHL-FF-D2": "155" } -> for Tire Pressures/Dates
```

**Final JSONB Payload (`items` array):**
```json
[
  {
    "id": "CHL-FF-D2",
    "item": "Record NLG Tire #1 Pressure",
    "eng": true,
    "tech": false,
    "comment": null,
    "meta_value": "155",
    "meta_unit": "psi"
  }
]
```

