## 3. Dynamic Email HTML Builder Rendering

The Vercel `/api/submit.js` endpoint will be updated to parse and render the polymorphic `items` JSON array. 

When generating the HTML table rows:
```javascript
const rows = (r.items || []).map((i) => {
  // Base description & comments
  let text = escape(i.item);
  if (i.comment) {
    text += `<br><span style="color:#666;font-size:12px">&#8627; ${escape(i.comment)}</span>`;
  }
  
  // Dynamic Meta Entry (Readings & Dates)
  if (i.meta_value) {
    const unit = i.meta_unit ? ` ${escape(i.meta_unit)}` : "";
    text += `<br><span style="color:#003B73;font-size:13px;font-weight:bold;">
               ↳ Recorded Value: ${escape(i.meta_value)}${unit}
             </span>`;
  }

  return `<tr>
    <td style="padding:4px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee">${text}</td>
    <td style="text-align:center;border-bottom:1px solid #eee">${i.eng ? "\u2713" : ""}</td>
    <td style="text-align:center;border-bottom:1px solid #eee">${i.tech ? "\u2713" : ""}</td>
  </tr>`;
}).join("");
```
This ensures the Resend email cleanly displays Gulfstream's pass/fail toggles alongside Challenger's tire pressure readings and Hawker's daily-only task indicators.
